## Outward Search v2 — Architecture

### Foundation Tables
- `source_registry` — evolved from existing table, added: adapter_type, tier, rate_limit_per_hour, cooldown_minutes, health tracking (last_success_at, consecutive_failures, auto_disabled_at)
- `dealer_entitlements` — per-account quota: plan_tier (free/pro/enterprise), max_searches_per_day, max_sources_per_search, allowed_source_tiers, daily reset
- `outward_search_runs` — full telemetry: intent, sources queried, results by source, cache hits, quota snapshots, duration

### Shared Modules (`_shared/outward-search/`)
- `types.ts` — ParsedIntent, AdapterResult, OutwardSearchAdapter interface, QuotaCheckResult, SearchRunRecord, constants
- `intent-parser.ts` — LLM parser (gemini-2.5-flash-lite) + regex fallback
- `quota.ts` — checkQuota() + incrementUsage(); operator/cron bypass, daily reset, cooldown filtering
- `adapters/internal-db.ts` — InternalDbAdapter: queries vehicle_listings with badge filtering + scoring

### Edge Function: `run-outward-search-v2`
Orchestration flow:
1. Demand gating (skip if ≥5 internal results + non-urgent)
2. Quota check via checkQuota()
3. Intent parsing (structured filters → LLM → regex fallback)
4. Cache check (3-hour, search_cache table)
5. Adapter dispatch (iterates eligible sources from registry)
6. Score + sort + cap at 30 results
7. Increment usage
8. Write cache
9. Log telemetry to outward_search_runs

### Adapter Contract
Any new source adapter implements `OutwardSearchAdapter`:
- `sourceKey: string`
- `search(intent, config, signal): Promise<AdapterResult[]>`
- Registered in ADAPTERS map in v2 index.ts

### Source Tiers
- `free`: internal_db, auction sources (pickles, manheim, grays, slattery, f3, aav)
- `premium`: carsales, autotrader, drive, carsguide, gumtree, facebook (manus adapter)

### Quota Defaults
- Free: 5 searches/day, 3 sources/search, free tier only
- Operator/cron: unlimited, all sources
- Anonymous: free tier sources only, no usage tracking

